<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-America Online view raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-America Online view raised.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- EVEREN Securities Inc said Thursday it raised its earnings estimate on America Online Inc for the third quarter ended March 31 to a loss of $0.10 from a loss of $0.15.</p>
<p>-- AOL's resumption of marketing efforts now, instead of at the end of April, led to the change, analyst Anthony Blenk said in a report.</p>
<p>-- &quot;We take this to mean that the company has been able to resolve its capacity problems sooner than we had originally expected,&quot; Blenk said.</p>
<p>-- He also said he believes a merger with CompuServe Corp is a distinct possibility.</p>
<p>-- America Online was up 1-1/4 at 46-3/8.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
